<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && \old(this.get(key)) == \result;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && \result != null;</code>

This assert statement checks that if the key was previously in the map (`\old(this.containsKey(key))`), then after the `remove` operation, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value returned by the `remove` operation is not `null` (`\result != null`). Note that the condition `\result != null` is included to handle the case where the key was present and had a non-null value. If the key was present but had a null value, the assertion would still hold because the key would no longer be in the map.
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && \old(this.get(key)) == \result;</code>
